    "Both use complete finite native100–400m positive signed-integral selection and core>10cm/s,held90degree eastward through depth. There is no surface-speed qualification. First southern native tie wins;selected gate/support-edge maxima remain unresolved without weaker interior replacement. Sensitivity layers have their own qualifying seed at the same selected column. No thermal fields or gates apply.",
    "Pacific NSCC155–125W/2.5–6N is a partial northern Tsuchiya-jet-context reach,distinct from equatorial EUC,shallower NECC,southern jets and the weak deep western-Pacific NEUC multi-jet system. Historical Johnson2002 means and Rowe2000 archives do not validate2022 axes or boundaries. NSCC/NECC same-sign connections remain possible;no independent branch or water-mass assignment is established.",
    "Atlantic NEUC40–30W/2–5N is partial thermocline-current context. Sivkov2021 regional setting and primary indexed Schott2003 35W text distinguish it from surface pathways and EUC. Source100–300m feeding layers,pressure/density domains,transport limits and historical cruise support are not current edges or2022 observations. NBC retroflection,NECC,northern intermediate current and detached eddies remain separate targets.",
    "Source Li2018 describes weak western-Pacific NEUC jets requiring long averaging. They are not relabeled as the Pacific NSCC or inferred from these two snapshots. Their separate300/450/600m upper-boundary references remain unchanged;latent mean-jet collection is still needed.",
    "All windows/stops are OSW exploratory choices rather than source axes,widths,errors or seasonal extremes. Geographic maxima may be neighboring/mesoscale flow. Neither100m nor400m bounds connected searches on full native0–5000m. Missing/bed/domain support censors and finite adjacent brackets are required. Upper/lower depths,statuses,supported bounds and paired span remain distinct;paired model span is not physical thickness.",
    "New interval-only collector/audit reuse frozen preflight,native component/geometry math,bounded exact-read retries and interval/connected-layer helpers. Older validated source/helper bytes remain unchanged. Exact transport ledger reserves future first attempts before retries;counts describe requested/decoded values rather than wire traffic or precision. All numerical acquisition,audits,geometry/contours and tests ran sequentially in cloud on one idle CPU.",
    "Local work prepared code,reviewed primary text/metadata,checked hashes and retained exact artifacts. No local numerical field processing/tests or runtime/UI/browser work. Original transport/file/inline/aggregate caps remain unchanged. Canonical registerv48,inventoryv18 and eddy baseline102size-referenced/34unresolved stay unchanged by source retention.",
